umping in on you the solution  use your and tires the opponent landing  a lot of counter hits on you stop trying  to attack after you block and serve your  movement number 6 use everything  Oh mostly your moves are an extension of  yourself use them not just for damage  but for answers to specific situations I  made the mistake of relying on strong  attacks our punch and heartache over  weaker ones like light punch and light  kick I wanted to hurt the opponent by  capitalizing on every opportunity with  the most damage but this just restricts  your game your normals and special moves  are more than just tools were damaged  they can be applied to a number  situations restricting your opponent's  options or asking them by constant  sticking out something in their space or  stuffing their attacks number seven the  rhythm avoid falling into a predictable  rhythm by using a set pattern do  something unexpected even crazy to throw  off your opponent's mindset a pattern  has a predictable rhythm for example  mindlessly chucking fireballs without  changing your timing or position is a  pattern easily exploitable by your  opponent in this case stepping a few  paces back before throwing a barbell or  pausing for every second is enough to  change the rhythm number eight pattern  recognition recognizing patterns  strengthens your ability to adapt to  anticipate and to have a quick answer  for a disadvantaged situation rhythm is  important role encounter recognition the  required skill for any competitive game  by recognizing patterns you can come up  with an answer to the obstacle stay one  step ahead of your opponent number nine  fear just being in someone's immediate  space is enough to manipulate their  behavior when people are scared they'll  either fight or flee in fighting games  this means you're probably jump back  and/or walk away from the opponent or  hit a bunch of buttons to get the  opponent out of your surrounding space  use this to influence your opponent's  deci